IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mv-act`

-- Motor Vehicles (Third-Party Risks and Compensation) Act 1960 (Singapore)
-- -- ss 5 to 8 and ss 10 to 16.
--
-- The rest of the Act, after s 3, s 4 and s 9 in mv-act.l4. Everything here
-- serves one purpose: to stop the insurance from failing the injured third
-- party. Each section removes a way the cover could otherwise be defeated --
-- by an agreement with the passenger (s 5), by a condition in the policy
-- (s 7), by a restriction on who may drive or how (s 8), by the insured's
-- bankruptcy (ss 10-13), or by a settlement behind the third party's back
-- (s 14).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No
-- pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 6's procedural machinery for settlement payments beyond the
-- routing rule, s 17 (deposits), s 18A (solicitation), ss 19-20 (the Public
-- Trustee's powers), s 21 (power to amend sums), s 22 (securities), s 23
-- (penalty), s 24 (rules), and the Schedule of territories.

§ `Motor Vehicles Act 1960 -- sections 5 to 16`

§§ `5 -- Agreements with a passenger are of no effect`

-- s 5(1): where s 3 requires cover and another person is carried in or upon the
-- vehicle, "any ANTECEDENT AGREEMENT OR UNDERSTANDING between them (WHETHER
-- INTENDED TO BE LEGALLY BINDING OR NOT) is OF NO EFFECT so far as it purports
-- or might be held -- (a) to negative or restrict any such liability of the user
-- ... as is required by section 4 to be covered ...; or (b) to impose any
-- conditions with respect to the enforcement of any such liability."
--
-- s 5(2): "The fact that a person so carried ... has WILLINGLY ACCEPTED as the
-- person's the risk of negligence on the part of the user is NOT to be treated
-- as negativing any such liability."
--
-- s 5(3): being carried includes "entering or getting on to, or ALIGHTING
-- FROM"; and an antecedent agreement is one made "at any time BEFORE THE
-- LIABILITY AROSE".
--
-- Three things worth noticing: the agreement need not be binding to be caught,
-- volenti is expressly excluded, and the protection reaches the moment of
-- getting in and out, not only the journey.
DECLARE PassengerAgreement HAS
    `section 3 required cover for this use`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was carried in or upon the vehicle, including entering, getting on to or alighting from it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was an agreement or understanding between them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was intended to be legally binding`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was made before the liability arose`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it purports to negative or restrict the liability required to be covered` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `it purports to impose conditions on the enforcement of that liability` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `the person willingly accepted the risk of the user's negligence` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (2)

GIVEN `the agreement` IS A PassengerAgreement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement is of no effect under section 5(1)` IF
        `section 5 is engaged` `the agreement`
    AND `the agreement does one of the two forbidden things` `the agreement`

GIVEN `the agreement` IS A PassengerAgreement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5 is engaged` IF
        `the agreement`'s `section 3 required cover for this use`
    AND `the agreement`'s `the person was carried in or upon the vehicle, including entering, getting on to or alighting from it`
    AND `the agreement`'s `there was an agreement or understanding between them`
    AND `the agreement`'s `it was made before the liability arose`

GIVEN `the agreement` IS A PassengerAgreement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement does one of the two forbidden things` IF
        `the agreement`'s `it purports to negative or restrict the liability required to be covered`
    OR  `the agreement`'s `it purports to impose conditions on the enforcement of that liability`

-- s 5(2), stated on its own because it is a complete answer to a defence rather
-- than a condition of anything: willing acceptance of the risk never negatives
-- the liability.
GIVEN `the agreement` IS A PassengerAgreement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the liability is negatived by the passenger's acceptance of the risk` IF
    FALSE

§§ `7 -- Conditions in the policy are of no effect`

-- s 7(1): "Any condition in a policy or security ... providing that NO LIABILITY
-- ARISES ... or that any liability so arising CEASES in the event of some
-- specified thing being done or omitted to be done AFTER THE HAPPENING OF THE
-- EVENT giving rise to a claim ... is OF NO EFFECT in connection with such
-- claims as are mentioned in section 4(1)(b)."
--
-- The timing is the whole of it. A condition about something to be done BEFORE
-- the accident -- keeping the vehicle roadworthy, say -- is untouched. Only
-- conditions biting on post-accident conduct are struck down, and only as
-- against the third party.
--
-- s 7(2): the insurer may still require the insured to REPAY what it has paid
-- out to third parties. So the condition fails against the third party and
-- survives against the insured.
DECLARE PolicyCondition HAS
    `the condition provides that no liability arises or that liability ceases` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it operates on something done or omitted AFTER the event giving rise to the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim is one mentioned in section 4(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the condition requires the insured to repay the insurer sums applied to third party claims` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the condition` IS A PolicyCondition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the condition is of no effect under section 7(1)` IF
        `the condition`'s `the condition provides that no liability arises or that liability ceases`
    AND `the condition`'s `it operates on something done or omitted AFTER the event giving rise to the claim`
    AND `the condition`'s `the claim is one mentioned in section 4(1)(b)`
    AND NOT `the condition`'s `the condition requires the insured to repay the insurer sums applied to third party claims`

§§ `8 -- Restrictions on the scope of the policy are of no effect`

-- s 8(1): where a certificate has been issued, "so much of the policy as
-- purports to RESTRICT the insurance of the persons insured by the policy by
-- reference to any of the following matters" is, as respects the s 4(1)(b)
-- liabilities, "OF NO EFFECT":
--   (a) the age or physical or mental condition of persons driving;
--   (b) the condition of the vehicle;
--   (c) the number of persons the vehicle carries;
--   (d) the weight or physical characteristics of the goods carried;
--   (e) the times at which or the areas within which the vehicle is used;
--   (f) the horsepower or value of the vehicle;
--   (g) the carrying of any particular apparatus;
--   (h) the carrying of any particular means of identification other than one
--       required by the Road Traffic Act 1961.
--
-- A CLOSED LIST of eight. A restriction by reference to anything else -- the
-- driver's licence class, or whether the vehicle was being used for hire --
-- stands.
--
-- s 8(3): a sum the insurer pays which is covered "BY VIRTUE ONLY OF THIS
-- SECTION" is recoverable from the insured. Same shape as s 7(2): the
-- restriction fails against the third party and the insured bears it.
DECLARE RestrictionGround IS ONE OF
    `the age or physical or mental condition of persons driving the vehicle`   -- (a)
    `the condition of the vehicle`                                             -- (b)
    `the number of persons that the vehicle carries`                           -- (c)
    `the weight or physical characteristics of the goods that the vehicle carries` -- (d)
    `the times at which or the areas within which the vehicle is used`         -- (e)
    `the horsepower or value of the vehicle`                                   -- (f)
    `the carrying on the vehicle of any particular apparatus`                  -- (g)
    `the carrying of a means of identification not required by the Road Traffic Act 1961` -- (h)
    `some ground outside the section 8(1) list`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A RestrictionGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground is in the section 8(1) list` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `some ground outside the section 8(1) list` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A RestrictionGround
    , `a certificate of insurance has been issued under section 4(9)` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the liability is one required to be covered by section 4(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the restriction is of no effect under section 8(1)` IF
        `a certificate of insurance has been issued under section 4(9)`
    AND `the liability is one required to be covered by section 4(1)(b)`
    AND `the ground is in the section 8(1) list` `the ground`

-- s 8(3) and s 7(2) together: the insurer pays the third party and recovers
-- from the insured. The cover is for the victim's benefit, not the driver's.
GIVEN `the sum was covered by the policy by virtue only of section 8` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insurer may recover the sum from the insured` IF
    `the sum was covered by the policy by virtue only of section 8`

§§ `10 to 13 -- The insured's insolvency does not reach the third party`

-- s 10(1): where the insured is insured against third-party liabilities, then on
--   (a) the insured becoming bankrupt or compounding with creditors; or
--   (b) for a company: a winding up order or voluntary winding up resolution, a
--       receiver or manager being appointed, or a debenture holder taking
--       possession under a floating charge,
-- "if either BEFORE OR AFTER that event any such liability ... is incurred by
-- the insured the insured's rights against the insurer under the policy in
-- respect of the liability are, DESPITE ANYTHING IN ANY WRITTEN LAW TO THE
-- CONTRARY, TO BE TRANSFERRED TO AND VEST IN THE THIRD PARTY".
--
-- The third party takes the insured's rights directly. The policy proceeds
-- never enter the estate, so the other creditors never see them.
DECLARE InsolvencyEvent IS ONE OF
    `the insured became bankrupt or compounded with creditors`      -- (1)(a)
    `a winding up order was made or a voluntary winding up resolution passed` -- (1)(b)(i)
    `a receiver or manager of the company was duly appointed`       -- (1)(b)(ii)
    `a debenture holder took possession under a floating charge`    -- (1)(b)(iii)
    `no insolvency event`

GIVEN `the event` IS AN InsolvencyEvent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 10(1) event has happened` IF
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `no insolvency event` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the event` IS AN InsolvencyEvent
    , `the insured is insured against the liability under a policy issued for the purposes of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the liability was incurred, whether before or after the event` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insured's rights against the insurer vest in the third party` IF
        `a section 10(1) event has happened` `the event`
    AND `the insured is insured against the liability under a policy issued for the purposes of this Act`
    AND `the liability was incurred, whether before or after the event`

-- s 12: once the rights have transferred, "NO AGREEMENT made between the
-- insurer and the insured after liability has been incurred ... AND AFTER THE
-- COMMENCEMENT of the bankruptcy or winding up ... NOR ANY WAIVER, ASSIGNMENT
-- OR OTHER DISPOSITION made by, or PAYMENT MADE TO, the insured ... is
-- EFFECTIVE TO DEFEAT OR AFFECT the rights transferred".
--
-- Both conditions are needed: after the liability AND after the commencement.
DECLARE PostTransferDealing HAS
    `an agreement, waiver, assignment, disposition or payment was made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was made after the liability was incurred` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was made after the commencement of the bankruptcy or winding up` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A PostTransferDealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing cannot defeat the third party's rights` IF
        `the dealing`'s `an agreement, waiver, assignment, disposition or payment was made`
    AND `the dealing`'s `it was made after the liability was incurred`
    AND `the dealing`'s `it was made after the commencement of the bankruptcy or winding up`

-- s 13(1): the happening of a s 10 event "DOES NOT ... AFFECT ANY SUCH
-- LIABILITY of that person as is required to be covered by a policy under
-- section 4(1)(b)."
--
-- So the liability survives the insolvency as well as the rights against the
-- insurer. The third party keeps both routes.
GIVEN `the event` IS AN InsolvencyEvent
    , `a certificate of insurance has been issued under section 4(9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the liability survives the insolvency event` IF
    `a certificate of insurance has been issued under section 4(9)`

§§ `11 -- The duty to say whether there was a policy`

-- s 11(1): "Any person against whom a claim is made in respect of any such
-- liability as is required to be covered by a policy under section 4(1)(b) MUST
-- ON DEMAND by or on behalf of the person making the claim STATE whether or not
-- the person was insured ... OR WOULD HAVE BEEN SO INSURED IF THE INSURER HAD
-- NOT AVOIDED OR CANCELLED THE POLICY and if ... so insured give such
-- particulars ... as were specified in the certificate".
--
-- The second limb matters: a driver whose policy the insurer has avoided must
-- still disclose it. Otherwise the s 9 route -- which survives avoidance --
-- could never be found by the claimant.
DECLARE InformationDemand HAS
    `a claim was made in respect of a liability required to be covered by section 4(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a demand was made by or on behalf of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was insured in respect of that liability` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person would have been insured had the insurer not avoided or cancelled the policy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person stated whether or not they were insured` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person gave the particulars specified in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the demand` IS AN InformationDemand
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty under section 11(1) arises` IF
        `the demand`'s `a claim was made in respect of a liability required to be covered by section 4(1)(b)`
    AND `the demand`'s `a demand was made by or on behalf of the claimant`

GIVEN `the demand` IS AN InformationDemand
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `particulars are owed as well as a statement` IF
        `the demand`'s `the person was insured in respect of that liability`
    OR  `the demand`'s `the person would have been insured had the insurer not avoided or cancelled the policy`

GIVEN `the demand` IS AN InformationDemand
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has contravened section 11(1)` IF
        `the duty under section 11(1) arises` `the demand`
    AND `something owed was not given` `the demand`

GIVEN `the demand` IS AN InformationDemand
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `something owed was not given` IF
        NOT `the demand`'s `the person stated whether or not they were insured`
    OR  `particulars were owed and not given` `the demand`

GIVEN `the demand` IS AN InformationDemand
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `particulars were owed and not given` IF
        `particulars are owed as well as a statement` `the demand`
    AND NOT `the demand`'s `the person gave the particulars specified in the certificate`

§§ `14 -- No settlement behind the third party's back`

-- s 14(1): "NO SETTLEMENT by an insurer in respect of any claim which MIGHT be
-- made by a third party ... IS VALID UNLESS THE THIRD PARTY IS A PARTY TO THE
-- SETTLEMENT."
--
-- Note "might be made". The protection reaches a claim not yet brought, so an
-- insurer cannot buy off the insured before the victim has sued.
--
-- s 14(2): the policy "remains in force and available for third parties DESPITE
-- THE DEATH of any person insured ... AS IF THE INSURED PERSON WERE STILL
-- ALIVE."
GIVEN `the insurer settled a claim which might be made by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the third party was a party to the settlement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the settlement is invalid under section 14(1)` IF
        `the insurer settled a claim which might be made by a third party`
    AND NOT `the third party was a party to the settlement`

GIVEN `the insured person has died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the policy remains available to third parties` IF
    TRUE

§§ `15 -- Surrender of the certificate on cancellation`

-- s 15(1): where a certificate has been issued and the policy is cancelled by
-- mutual consent or under the policy, the person to whom the certificate was
-- issued must, "WITHIN 7 DAYS from the taking effect of the cancellation,
-- surrender the certificate to the insurer or, if it has been lost or
-- destroyed, make a statutory declaration to that effect."
--
-- This is the duty whose performance s 9(6)(c) turns into a bar on the third
-- party's recovery. The driver's 7 days decide whether the victim is paid.
`the surrender period in days` MEANS 7

DECLARE SurrenderFacts HAS
    `a certificate of insurance was issued under section 4(9)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days from the taking effect of the cancellation when that was done` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the facts` IS A SurrenderFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surrender duty under section 15(1) arises` IF
        `the facts`'s `a certificate of insurance was issued under section 4(9)`
    AND `the facts`'s `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A SurrenderFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has contravened section 15(1)` IF
        `the surrender duty under section 15(1) arises` `the facts`
    AND `the surrender was not made in time` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A SurrenderFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surrender was not made in time` IF
        NOT `the facts`'s `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made`
    OR  `the facts`'s `days from the taking effect of the cancellation when that was done`
            GREATER THAN `the surrender period in days`

-- s 15(2) and s 16(2): the same penalty in both -- a fine not exceeding $500,
-- and on a second or subsequent conviction a fine not exceeding $1,000 or
-- imprisonment not exceeding 6 months.
`the first conviction fine ceiling in dollars` MEANS 500
`the subsequent conviction fine ceiling in dollars` MEANS 1000
`the subsequent conviction imprisonment ceiling in months` MEANS 6

GIVEN `this is a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine in dollars` IS
    IF   `this is a second or subsequent conviction`
    THEN `the subsequent conviction fine ceiling in dollars`
    ELSE `the first conviction fine ceiling in dollars`

§§ `16 -- Production of the certificate`

-- s 16(1): a person driving on a road must, on being required by a police
-- officer, give their name and address, the owner's name and address, and
-- produce the certificate.
DECLARE ProductionDemand HAS
    `the person was driving a motor vehicle on a road` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a police officer required it`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person gave their own name and address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person gave the owner's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person produced the certificate`       IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the demand` IS A ProductionDemand
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has contravened section 16(1)` IF
        `the demand`'s `the person was driving a motor vehicle on a road`
    AND `the demand`'s `a police officer required it`
    AND `something required by section 16(1) was withheld` `the demand`

GIVEN `the demand` IS A ProductionDemand
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `something required by section 16(1) was withheld` IF
        NOT `the demand`'s `the person gave their own name and address`
    ..  NOT `the demand`'s `the person gave the owner's name and address`
    OR  NOT `the demand`'s `the person produced the certificate`
